+
+The implementation types in this table can be replaced for a project by adding a `mapstruct.properties` resource to
+the root of the mapping compilation classpath. Each replacement uses the fully-qualified interface and implementation
+names:
+
+[source, properties]
+----
+mapstruct.collectionImplementation.java.util.List=com.example.CapacityAwareList
+mapstruct.collectionImplementation.java.util.Map=com.example.OrderedMap
+----
+
+A different resource on the same classpath can be selected with the annotation processor option
+`mapstruct.configurationFile`, for example `-Amapstruct.configurationFile=META-INF/mapstruct/collections.properties`.
+An explicitly selected resource must exist. Configuration resources are read from the mapping compilation classpath,
+not from the annotation processor classpath.
+
+The configured implementation must be a publicly accessible concrete class assignable to the interface. It must
+preserve the interface's unbounded type parameters, expose a public no-argument constructor without checked
+exceptions, and have the same number of type parameters as the interface. If it also has a usable public `int`
+constructor, MapStruct passes the source size as its initial capacity. An applicable object factory takes precedence
+over a configured implementation.
+
+The configuration applies whenever MapStruct constructs that exact supported interface, including collection and map
+mapping methods, direct bean-property copies, and stream results. Unknown properties, unsupported interfaces, empty
+values, conflicting duplicate entries, and invalid implementation classes cause compilation to fail. Repeating the
+same property with the same value is allowed. Implementation classes may be part of the current compilation or be
+generated in a later annotation-processing round.
